        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the key quantities: Patricia has 4 barrels, each with a capacity of 7 gallons, and a faucet with a flow rate of 3.5 gallons per minute. The unknown I needed to find was the total time required to fill all barrels.\n\nFirst, I calculated the total volume needed to fill all barrels:\n\\[ \\text{Total Volume} = 4 \\text{ barrels} \\times 7 \\text{ gallons/barrel} = 28 \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\nNext, I used the flow rate of the faucet to determine the time required to fill this total volume:\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Total Volume}}{\\text{Flow Rate}} = \\frac{28 \\text{ gallons}}{3.5 \\text{ gallons/minute}} = 8 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTo verify this result, I considered that the flow rate of 3.5 gallons per minute means the faucet can fill 3.5 gallons every minute. Over 8 minutes, the faucet would fill:\n\\[ 3.5 \\text{ gallons/minute} \\times 8 \\text{ minutes} = 28 \\text{ gallons} \\]\nThis matches the total volume needed to fill all barrels, confirming my calculation.\n\nThe operation I would reuse is the formula for calculating time based on volume and flow rate, as it directly connects the given quantities to the unknown and is applicable in similar problems involving filling rates.\n\nFINAL: 8",
        "target_sha256": "2b01525b2f0719ec0a5b840e259d912dfe241639fc123c728769c83a5219df9a"
      }
    ],
