        "student_prefix_sha256": "664a12ab66c4a98596dcaf28d6a0d14e4019bdd048cfae98610a8cd7647ad545",
        "target": "Initially, the storage tank had 30,000 gallons of milk. Over 4 hours, 2,880 gallons/hour were pumped out, so 4 * 2,880 = 11,520 gallons were removed. This leaves 30,000 - 11,520 = 18,480 gallons. Then, over the next 7 hours, 1,500 gallons/hour were added, so 7 * 1,500 = 10,500 gallons were added. Adding this to the remaining milk gives 18,480 + 10,500 = 28,980 gallons. \n\nFINAL: 28980",
