          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "5b2af6df59d1c80637634ab4c4d41de0419be655cad45bda37e343ab65096c05",
        "target": "Given that Kevin can eat 64 wings in 8 minutes, we need to determine how many more wings per minute Alan must eat to surpass Kevin's record.\n\nFirst, calculate Kevin's rate of eating wings:\n\\[ \\text{Kevin's rate} = \\frac{64 \\text{ wings}}{8 \\text{ minutes}} = 8 \\text{ wings per minute} \\]\n\nAlan currently eats at a rate of 5 wings per minute. To beat Kevin's record, Alan needs to eat more than 8 wings per minute. Therefore, the additional rate Alan needs is:\n\\[ \\text{Additional rate needed} = 8 \\text{ wings per minute} - 5 \\text{ wings per minute} = 3 \\text{ wings per minute} \\]\n\nAlan must eat 3 more wings per minute to beat Kevin's record.\n\nFINAL: 3",
